IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `eia-core-interpretation`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Part VIII.4 (Employment Insurance Emergency Response Benefit),
-- Interpretation (s 153.5) and Application (s 153.6). Written by piece ei6 (Sonnet 5.5) on 2026-10-24.
-- Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30; nothing here is
-- claimed to be verified against the official text.
--
-- Seat: a person who has lost work or cannot work and asks whether they qualify for benefits (here, whether they are
-- a "claimant" for the emergency response benefit of March 15 to October 3, 2020).
--
-- Every rule takes plain facts as its own GIVEN parameters, because the stable binary rejects a GIVEN on a section.
-- "Initial claim for benefits" (s 153.5(1)(c)) has the meaning of s 6(1) (piece ei1): wherever Part VIII.4 needs it,
-- it is a plain input (BOOLEAN, or the DATE the claim was made); this module has nothing to compute for it.

§ `Section 153.5(1) - definitions for Part VIII.4`

-- A definition carrier (pattern 7.5): the words of the definition, nothing to compute. The facts it qualifies are
-- the BOOLEAN inputs below that are worded "for reasons related to COVID-19".
-- src:2768 | (a) COVID-19 means the coronavirus disease 2019;
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.5(1)(a) (src:2768)
GIVETH A STRING
`s 153.5(1)(a) COVID-19` MEANS "the coronavirus disease 2019"

§ `Section 153.5(2) and (3) - the claimant of Part VIII.4`

-- The periods of paragraphs (b) to (d), carried as values (dates are data).
-- src:2774 | (b) who could have had a benefit period established on or after March 15, 2020 with respect to any of the benefits referred to in paragraph (3)(a);
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.5(2)(b) (src:2774)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 153.5(2)(b) the first day on which a benefit period could have been established` MEANS YearMonthDay 2020 3 15

-- src:2775 | (c) who is unable to start working for reasons related to COVID-19 and to whom, at any time during the period beginning on December 29, 2019 and ending on October 3, 2020, at least one benefit referred to in paragraph (3)(b) has been paid or was payable, if, during that period
-- src:2779 | (d) who is unable to start working for reasons related to COVID-19 and to whom, at any time during the period beginning on December 29, 2019 and ending on October 3, 2020, at least one benefit referred to in paragraph (3)(c) has been paid or was payable, if, during that period
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.5(2)(c), (d) (src:2775) (src:2779)
GIVETH A `Period of days`
`s 153.5(2)(c) and (d) the period in which a benefit was paid or payable` MEANS
    `Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2019 12 29), (YearMonthDay 2020 10 3)

-- Whether a day falls in that period. Paragraphs (c) and (d) speak of what happened "at any time during the period":
-- a caller who has a date for it asks this; the rules below take the answer as a BOOLEAN so that a person can state it.
-- src:2775 | (c) who is unable to start working for reasons related to COVID-19 and to whom, at any time during the period beginning on December 29, 2019 and ending on October 3, 2020, at least one benefit referred to in paragraph (3)(b) has been paid or was payable, if, during that period
-- src:2779 | (d) who is unable to start working for reasons related to COVID-19 and to whom, at any time during the period beginning on December 29, 2019 and ending on October 3, 2020, at least one benefit referred to in paragraph (3)(c) has been paid or was payable, if, during that period
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.5(2)(c), (d) (src:2775) (src:2779)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 153.5(2)(c) and (d) the day falls within the period` MEANS
    `the day` day `falls within` `s 153.5(2)(c) and (d) the period in which a benefit was paid or payable`

-- (3): the benefits referred to in paragraphs (2)(b) to (d). A benefit is named by the Part it is provided under and
-- the number of its section (sections 22 to 24 include 23.1, 23.2 and 23.3, which lie between 23 and 24).
-- src:2784 | (3) The benefits referred to in paragraphs (2)(b) to (d) are
-- src:2785 | (a) with respect to a claimant referred to in paragraph (2)(b), benefits provided under section 152.03 or provided under Part I, other than those benefits provided under any of sections 22 to 24;
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.5(3)(a) (src:2784-2785)
GIVEN `the Part under which the benefit is provided` IS A `Part of the Act`
      `the number of the section under which the benefit is provided` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.5(3)(a) the benefit is referred to in paragraph (2)(b)` IF
        (   `the Part under which the benefit is provided` EQUALS `Part VII.1`
        AND `the number of the section under which the benefit is provided` EQUALS 152.03)
     OR (   `the Part under which the benefit is provided` EQUALS `Part I`
        AND NOT (   `the number of the section under which the benefit is provided` AT LEAST 22
                AND `the number of the section under which the benefit is provided` AT MOST 24))

-- src:2786 | (b) with respect to a claimant referred to in paragraph (2)(c), benefits provided under Part I, other than those benefits provided under any of sections 21 to 24; and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.5(3)(b) (src:2786)
GIVEN `the Part under which the benefit is provided` IS A `Part of the Act`
      `the number of the section under which the benefit is provided` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.5(3)(b) the benefit is referred to in paragraph (2)(c)` IF
        `the Part under which the benefit is provided` EQUALS `Part I`
    AND NOT (   `the number of the section under which the benefit is provided` AT LEAST 21
            AND `the number of the section under which the benefit is provided` AT MOST 24)

-- src:2787 | (c) with respect to a claimant referred to in paragraph (2)(d), benefits provided under the employment insurance scheme established under Part VIII.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.5(3)(c) (src:2787)
GIVEN `the Part under which the benefit is provided` IS A `Part of the Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.5(3)(c) the benefit is referred to in paragraph (2)(d)` IF
    `the Part under which the benefit is provided` EQUALS `Part VIII`

-- (2)(a): a person who ceases working, whether employed or self-employed, for reasons related to COVID-19.
-- src:2773 | (a) who ceases working, whether employed or self-employed, for reasons related to COVID-19;
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.5(2)(a) (src:2773)
GIVEN `ceases working, whether employed or self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `for reasons related to COVID-19` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.5(2)(a) claimant who ceases working for reasons related to COVID-19` IF
        `ceases working, whether employed or self-employed`
    AND `for reasons related to COVID-19`

-- (2)(b): a person who could have had a benefit period established on or after March 15, 2020 for a benefit in (3)(a).
-- src:2774 | (b) who could have had a benefit period established on or after March 15, 2020 with respect to any of the benefits referred to in paragraph (3)(a);
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.5(2)(b) (src:2774)
GIVEN `the day on which a benefit period could have been established` IS A DATE
      `the benefit is one referred to in paragraph (3)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.5(2)(b) claimant who could have had a benefit period established` IF
        `the day on which a benefit period could have been established` AT LEAST `s 153.5(2)(b) the first day on which a benefit period could have been established`
    AND `the benefit is one referred to in paragraph (3)(a)`

-- (2)(c): unable to start working for reasons related to COVID-19, and a benefit referred to in (3)(b) was paid or
-- payable at some time in the period, if in that period (i) the benefit period ended, (ii) all the benefits were
-- paid, or (iii) some could not be paid by virtue of subsection 12(6).
-- src:2775 | (c) who is unable to start working for reasons related to COVID-19 and to whom, at any time during the period beginning on December 29, 2019 and ending on October 3, 2020, at least one benefit referred to in paragraph (3)(b) has been paid or was payable, if, during that period
-- src:2776 | (i) the established benefit period of that person with respect to those benefits has ended,
-- src:2777 | (ii) all of those benefits have been paid to that person, or
-- src:2778 | (iii) some of those benefits cannot be paid to that person by virtue of subsection 12(6); or
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.5(2)(c) (src:2775-2778)
GIVEN `unable to start working for reasons related to COVID-19` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a benefit referred to in paragraph (3)(b) was paid or was payable at some time in the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in that period the established benefit period ended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in that period all of those benefits were paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in that period some of those benefits could not be paid by virtue of subsection 12(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.5(2)(c) claimant who is unable to start working after benefits under Part I` IF
        `unable to start working for reasons related to COVID-19`
    AND `a benefit referred to in paragraph (3)(b) was paid or was payable at some time in the period`
    AND (   `in that period the established benefit period ended`
         OR `in that period all of those benefits were paid`
         OR `in that period some of those benefits could not be paid by virtue of subsection 12(6)`)

-- (2)(d): the same for a benefit referred to in (3)(c), with subsection 8(18) of the Employment Insurance (Fishing)
-- Regulations (not among the inputs) in place of subsection 12(6).
-- src:2779 | (d) who is unable to start working for reasons related to COVID-19 and to whom, at any time during the period beginning on December 29, 2019 and ending on October 3, 2020, at least one benefit referred to in paragraph (3)(c) has been paid or was payable, if, during that period
-- src:2780 | (i) the established benefit period of that person with respect to those benefits has ended,
-- src:2781 | (ii) all of those benefits have been paid to that person, or
-- src:2782 | (iii) some of those benefits cannot be paid to that person by virtue of subsection 8(18) of the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.5(2)(d) (src:2779-2782)
GIVEN `unable to start working for reasons related to COVID-19` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a benefit referred to in paragraph (3)(c) was paid or was payable at some time in the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in that period the established benefit period ended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in that period all of those benefits were paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in that period some of those benefits could not be paid by virtue of subsection 8(18) of the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.5(2)(d) claimant who is unable to start working after benefits under Part VIII` IF
        `unable to start working for reasons related to COVID-19`
    AND `a benefit referred to in paragraph (3)(c) was paid or was payable at some time in the period`
    AND (   `in that period the established benefit period ended`
         OR `in that period all of those benefits were paid`
         OR `in that period some of those benefits could not be paid by virtue of subsection 8(18) of the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations`)

-- (2): paragraphs (a) to (d) are alternatives. The "or" ends paragraph (c), and s 153.9(1) treats (b), (c) and (d)
-- as separate routes (fork F-ei6-1 in NOTES.md).
-- src:2772 | (2) For the purposes of this Part, claimant means a person
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.5(2) (src:2772)
GIVEN `a claimant under paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a claimant under paragraph (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a claimant under paragraph (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a claimant under paragraph (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.5(2) claimant within the meaning of Part VIII.4` IF
       `a claimant under paragraph (a)`
    OR `a claimant under paragraph (b)`
    OR `a claimant under paragraph (c)`
    OR `a claimant under paragraph (d)`

§ `Section 153.6 - other provisions of the Act and Regulations that apply`

-- A provision is named by the instrument, the Part of the Act that holds it (ignored for the Regulations) and its
-- section number and, if it is a subsection, the number of the subsection: 42(1) is section 42, subsection JUST 1.
-- src:2791 | 153.6 (1) In the case of a claim made for the employment insurance emergency response benefit, the following provisions apply in respect of the employment insurance emergency response benefit, subject to the adaptations set out in subsection (2) and in sections 153.1301 to 153.13091:
-- src:2792 | (a) subsections 42(1) and (2) and sections 43, 44, 47, 50 and 52;
-- src:2793 | (b) the provisions of Part II;
-- src:2794 | (c) the provisions of Part III and IV;
-- src:2795 | (d) the provisions of Part VI, except subsections 112(3) and 114(2) and sections 115 and 140; and
-- src:2796 | (e) section 27 and subsections 92(1) to (5) and (8) of the Employment Insurance Regulations.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.6(1) (src:2791-2796)
DECLARE `ei6 Provision cited in section 153.6` HAS
    `ei6 provision of the Regulations`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `ei6 Part of the Act that holds the provision`  IS A `Part of the Act`
    `ei6 number of the section of the provision`    IS A NUMBER
    `ei6 number of the subsection of the provision` IS A MAYBE NUMBER

-- (1)(a): subsections 42(1) and (2) and sections 43, 44, 47, 50 and 52.
-- src:2792 | (a) subsections 42(1) and (2) and sections 43, 44, 47, 50 and 52;
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.6(1)(a) (src:2792)
GIVEN p IS A `ei6 Provision cited in section 153.6`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.6(1)(a) the provision is one of subsections 42(1) and (2) and sections 43, 44, 47, 50 and 52` IF
        NOT (p's `ei6 provision of the Regulations`)
    AND (   (    p's `ei6 number of the section of the provision` EQUALS 42
             AND (p's `ei6 number of the subsection of the provision` EQUALS JUST 1 OR p's `ei6 number of the subsection of the provision` EQUALS JUST 2))
         OR elem (p's `ei6 number of the section of the provision`) (LIST 43, 44, 47, 50, 52))

-- (1)(b), (c): the provisions of Part II, and of Parts III and IV.
-- src:2793 | (b) the provisions of Part II;
-- src:2794 | (c) the provisions of Part III and IV;
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.6(1)(b), (c) (src:2793-2794)
GIVEN p IS A `ei6 Provision cited in section 153.6`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.6(1)(b) and (c) the provision is one of Parts II, III and IV` IF
        NOT (p's `ei6 provision of the Regulations`)
    AND (   p's `ei6 Part of the Act that holds the provision` EQUALS `Part II`
         OR p's `ei6 Part of the Act that holds the provision` EQUALS `Part III`
         OR p's `ei6 Part of the Act that holds the provision` EQUALS `Part IV`)

-- (1)(d): the provisions of Part VI, except subsections 112(3) and 114(2) and sections 115 and 140.
-- src:2795 | (d) the provisions of Part VI, except subsections 112(3) and 114(2) and sections 115 and 140; and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.6(1)(d) (src:2795)
GIVEN p IS A `ei6 Provision cited in section 153.6`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.6(1)(d) the provision is one of Part VI, except subsections 112(3) and 114(2) and sections 115 and 140` IF
        NOT (p's `ei6 provision of the Regulations`)
    AND p's `ei6 Part of the Act that holds the provision` EQUALS `Part VI`
    AND NOT (   (p's `ei6 number of the section of the provision` EQUALS 112 AND p's `ei6 number of the subsection of the provision` EQUALS JUST 3)
             OR (p's `ei6 number of the section of the provision` EQUALS 114 AND p's `ei6 number of the subsection of the provision` EQUALS JUST 2)
             OR elem (p's `ei6 number of the section of the provision`) (LIST 115, 140))

-- (1)(e): section 27 and subsections 92(1) to (5) and (8) of the Employment Insurance Regulations.
-- src:2796 | (e) section 27 and subsections 92(1) to (5) and (8) of the Employment Insurance Regulations.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.6(1)(e) (src:2796)
GIVEN p IS A `ei6 Provision cited in section 153.6`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.6(1)(e) the provision is section 27 or one of subsections 92(1) to (5) and (8) of the Regulations` IF
        p's `ei6 provision of the Regulations`
    AND (   p's `ei6 number of the section of the provision` EQUALS 27
         OR (    p's `ei6 number of the section of the provision` EQUALS 92
             AND (   elem (p's `ei6 number of the subsection of the provision`) (LIST JUST 1, JUST 2, JUST 3, JUST 4, JUST 5)
                  OR p's `ei6 number of the subsection of the provision` EQUALS JUST 8)))

-- (1) with (3): the provisions of (1) apply, and no other provision applies unless a contrary intention appears;
-- the definitions of subsection 2(1) apply, for greater certainty.
-- src:2791 | 153.6 (1) In the case of a claim made for the employment insurance emergency response benefit, the following provisions apply in respect of the employment insurance emergency response benefit, subject to the adaptations set out in subsection (2) and in sections 153.1301 to 153.13091:
-- src:2792 | (a) subsections 42(1) and (2) and sections 43, 44, 47, 50 and 52;
-- src:2793 | (b) the provisions of Part II;
-- src:2794 | (c) the provisions of Part III and IV;
-- src:2795 | (d) the provisions of Part VI, except subsections 112(3) and 114(2) and sections 115 and 140; and
-- src:2796 | (e) section 27 and subsections 92(1) to (5) and (8) of the Employment Insurance Regulations.
-- src:2803 | (3) No other provision of this Act or of any regulations made under it applies in respect of a claim for the employment insurance emergency response benefit unless a contrary intention appears. However, for greater certainty, the definitions set out in subsection 2(1) apply in this Part.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.6(1), (3) (src:2791-2796) (src:2803)
GIVEN p IS A `ei6 Provision cited in section 153.6`
      `it is a definition set out in subsection 2(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.6 the provision applies in respect of a claim for the emergency response benefit` IF
       `s 153.6(1)(a) the provision is one of subsections 42(1) and (2) and sections 43, 44, 47, 50 and 52` p
    OR `s 153.6(1)(b) and (c) the provision is one of Parts II, III and IV` p
    OR `s 153.6(1)(d) the provision is one of Part VI, except subsections 112(3) and 114(2) and sections 115 and 140` p
    OR `s 153.6(1)(e) the provision is section 27 or one of subsections 92(1) to (5) and (8) of the Regulations` p
    OR `it is a definition set out in subsection 2(1)`
    OR `a contrary intention appears`

-- (2): the provisions of (1)(a), (d) and (e) are adapted; those of (b) and (c) (Parts II, III and IV) are not.
-- src:2798 | (2) A provision referred to in paragraph (1)(a), (d) or (e) is adapted
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.6(2) (src:2798)
GIVEN p IS A `ei6 Provision cited in section 153.6`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.6(2) the provision is adapted for the emergency response benefit` IF
       `s 153.6(1)(a) the provision is one of subsections 42(1) and (2) and sections 43, 44, 47, 50 and 52` p
    OR `s 153.6(1)(d) the provision is one of Part VI, except subsections 112(3) and 114(2) and sections 115 and 140` p
    OR `s 153.6(1)(e) the provision is section 27 or one of subsections 92(1) to (5) and (8) of the Regulations` p

-- (2)(a): a definition carrier; the person is the claimant of s 153.5(2) and the benefit is the one of this Part.
-- src:2799 | (a) to refer, in respect of claimants and the benefits to which it refers, to the claimant within the meaning of this Part and the employment insurance emergency response benefit provided under this Part;
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.6(2)(a) (src:2799)
GIVETH A STRING
`s 153.6(2)(a) how an adapted provision reads a reference to claimants and benefits` MEANS
    "the claimant within the meaning of Part VIII.4 and the employment insurance emergency response benefit provided under Part VIII.4"

-- (2)(b): in the English version "entitled" and its other forms mean "eligible" under s 153.9: an adapted provision
-- that turns on entitlement turns on eligibility.
-- src:2800 | (b) so that any reference, in the English version, to “entitled” and other parts of speech and grammatical forms of the same word means “eligible” under section 153.9; and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.6(2)(b) (src:2800)
GIVEN `eligible for the emergency response benefit under section 153.9` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.6(2)(b) the claimant is entitled for the purposes of an adapted provision` IF
    `eligible for the emergency response benefit under section 153.9`

-- (2)(c): a definition carrier.
-- src:2801 | (c) so that any reference to the regulations made under the authority of this Act is to be read without that reference.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.6(2)(c) (src:2801)
GIVETH A STRING
`s 153.6(2)(c) how an adapted provision reads a reference to regulations made under the Act` MEANS
    "the reference to the regulations made under the authority of the Act is read without that reference"
